{"id": "37858911-babe-4a29-8e85-f7ef12b57fa5", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T06:45:34.975000", "source": "user", "parent_id": "f893382d-6bc0-41fd-898f-33c2f593fc5d", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Initial inspection request — design-only task, no execution required yet. I need the following from you before I authorize the main design work, and nothing more at this stage. The deliverable is a finalized experimental design with rationale, controls, analysis plan, and feasibility assessment; benchmarks are not run by me or you in this environment, and the bubblewrap sandbox is a scratch surface, not a training rig. The repo at /workspace is the only inspection target; do not assume availability of any dataset, framework, or model weights unless you find them on disk. Reports are claims, not evidence, so cite paths when you state what is present. Treat the markers below as a checklist, not a template to fill in mechanically. Focus on what is actually relevant to the question: whether BAdam's per-step update (the learning perturbation) shares Adam's heavy-tailed singular value spectrum and effective rank across transformer modules during finetuning, where the comparability is per-module and per-layer rather than a single scalar. (1) Repository inspection: list the contents of /workspace with a shallow tree and note which subdirectories, if any, contain existing BAdam / Adam implementations, any prior spectral analysis code, configuration files, or pre-downloaded model/tokenizer checkpoints. Flag any mismatch between what is on disk and what the question implicitly requires (base model checkpoint, finetuning dataset, evaluation harness). (2) Proposed approach: a one- to two-paragraph sketch of the experimental design only — base model selection and size, finetuning task and dataset, optimizer variants to compare (full-parameter Adam vs. BAdam with a stated block partition policy, plus at least one rationale for that policy), which transformer modules are instrumented (embeddings, attention Q/K/V/O projections, MLP up/gate/down, LayerNorms if linearized, head if present), the update-extraction protocol (sampling cadence across steps, warm-up and steady-state separation, handling of bias-corrected moments vs. raw moments for BAdam), and the spectral analysis procedure (SVD stability control in low precision, PSD safety for non-square weight matrices via Gram matrix for transformers ' effective rank, power-law tail fit on the empirical singular distribution, plus a non-parametric heavy-tail diagnostic such as tail index or rolling QQ against a Marchenko–Pastur reference, and a comparator metric against an isotropic Gaussian null). Do not produce the full design yet. (3) Consequential assumptions and uncertainties: enumerate the setup choices you cannot verify from the source materials and that materially shape the design — expected empirical outcome, runtime/compute budget (GPU hours, wall-clock, storage for update snapshots), base-model size class (125M–1.3B is reasonable if unspecified), context length, finetuning horizon and step sampling density, BAdam's block size and which layers are blocked, whether weight decay and gradient clipping are matched across optimizers, dtype (fp32 vs. bf16/fp16 and where SVD is computed), and the statistical unit for the comparison (per-step snapshot, per-token, or aggregated over a window). Flag each as 'assumed, needs confirmation' rather than presenting it as a design constraint. Keep the response concise and structured under the three headings above; I will respond with clarifications and an approve/continue decision at the next turn.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"- **Does BAdam produce a learning perturbation with a heavy-tailed singular value distribution and an effective rank comparable to that of Adam across various transformer modules during finetuning?**\\n\\n\\n- **Does BAdam produce a learning perturbation with a heavy-tailed singular value distribution and an effective rank comparable to that of Adam across various transformer modules during finetuning?**\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 24, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "kind": "MessageEvent", "source_event_index": 1}
