laim requires both failing the M-P null and exhibiting a Pareto tail index \\u03b1 \\u2272 3. Comparability is reported as per-(module, layer) deltas of erank, \\u03b1, M-P distance, and power-law slope, pooled across layers with layer index as a covariate, plus a paired test across matched (module, layer, step) pairs.\\n\\n## (3) Consequential assumptions and uncertainties\\n\\n1. Base-model size class 125M\\u20131.3B \\u2014 assumed, needs confirmation.\\n2. Specific base model identity (e.g., GPT-2 / Llama-3.2-1B / Pythia-1B) and tokenizer \\u2014 assumed, needs confirmation.\\n3. Finetuning task and dataset (default assumption: small SFT / domain-text corpus, ~50\\u2013500M training tokens; not present on disk and not fetchable) \\u2014 assumed, needs confirmation.\\n4. Context length (default assumption: 1024\\u20132048 tokens) \\u2014 assumed, needs confirmation.\\n5. Finetuning horizon and step sampling cadence (default assumption: ~10k total steps with 200-step warm-up logging and every-10 / every-50 logging thereafter; \\u2265 5 full round-robin sweeps of BAdam) \\u2014 assumed, needs confirmation.\\n6. BAdam block partition policy (default: primary = block size 1 round-robin; secondary = block size L/4 sliding by 1 layer/step) and whether BAdam updates only attention, only MLP, or all params within the active block (published variants differ here) \\u2014 assumed, needs confirmation; reference implementation source if reused rather than re-implemented.\\n7. Adam hyperparameters (\\u03b21, \\u03b22, \\u03b5, lr, schedule), weight-decay value and form (decoupled vs. L2), gradient-clipping norm \\u2014 assumed identical across optimizers, needs confirmation of exact values.\\n8. Update quantity compared \\u2014 default assumption: signed, bias-corrected `m\\u0302_t/(\\u221av\\u0302_t+\\u03b5)` for both optimizers (mechanism-comparable), with raw `\\u0394_t = -\\u03b7\\u00b7that` as the perturbation tensor; BAdam's moment state continues to drift in inactive blocks, so the equivalent extraction rule for frozen-block parameters must be defined \\u2014 assumed, needs confirmation.\\n9. Numeric dtype at extraction and SVD (default assumption: updates cast to fp32; SVD in fp64 accumulator for tail stability even if forward/backward is bf16/fp16) \\u2014 assumed, needs confirmation.\\n10. Non-square matrix handling (default assumption: use `W W\\u1d40` or `W\\u1d40 W` Gram singular values; effective rank computed on the smaller side; choice documented) \\u2014 assumed, needs confirmation.\\n11. Statistical unit for comparison (default assumption: per-(module, layer, step) snapshot, with layer-index as a covariate and step-window as a random effect; paired test at module-pair level) \\u2014 assumed, needs confirmation.\\n12. Compute / storage budget \\u2014 environment is CPU-only, 24 cores, no GPU, no network; running this at meaningful batch sizes without a GPU is borderline infeasible at any non-trivial scale, and the bubblewrap sandbox is \\\"scratch, not training rig\\\" per the researcher, so a separate runtime is implicitly required \\u2014 assumed, needs confirmation.\\n13. Reference \\\"BAdam\\\" semantics \\u2014 design assumes the published BAdam (block-adaptive Adam for memory-efficient finetuning, ~2023\\u20132024); if the researcher has a specific reference implementation or paper in mind, its exact block policy, parameter-selection rule, and moment-state handling must be cited and folded in \\u2014 assumed, needs confirmation.\\n14. Pre-existing materials \\u2014 none found on disk; if `track.md` becomes available or additional artefacts appear under `/workspace`, parts of this design may be anchored to them rather than treated as assumptions \\u2014 needs confirmation.\\n\", \"evidence\": \"Path-verified: `/workspace/` listing (`ls -la /workspace`) and `find /workspace -type f` both return only `/workspace/task.json`; directory tree at depth 3 contains only `/workspace` itself. System-wide search for any directory matching `*badam*`, `*adam*`, `*spectral*`, `*transformer*` under `/` (depth 4) found no project-relevant matches, only OS/internal Python and LibreOffice paths. No `.py`, `.safetensors`, `.bin`, or `.pt` files anywhere under `/workspace`. `documents.track.md` is referenced inside `task.json` but no file with that name exists at shallow depth under `/`. Environment fields in `task.json` declare `gpu_enabled: false`, `network: disabled`, `cpu_affinity_count: 24`, `python: python3`, `software_environment: system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled`.\", \"assumptions\": [\"[A1] Base-model size class 125M\\u20131.3B \\u2014 assumed, needs confirmation.</item>\\n<item>[A2] Specific base model identity (GPT-2 / Llama-3.2-1B / Pythia-1B-class) and tokenizer \\u2014 assumed, needs confirmation.</item>\\n<item>[A3] Finetuning task and dataset (default: small SFT/domain-text corpus, ~50\\u2013500M tokens; not on disk, not fetchable) \\u2014 assumed, needs confirmation.</item>\\n<item>[A4] Context length (default: 1024\\u20132048 tokens) \\u2014 assumed, needs confirmation.</item>\\n<item>[A5] Finetuning horizon and step sampling cadence (default: ~10k steps; every-step for 1..200; every 10/50 thereafter; \\u22655 round-robin sweeps) \\u2014 assumed, needs confirmation.</item>\\n<item>[A6] BAdam block partition policy (default: primary block-size-1 round-robin; secondary block-size L/4 sliding by 1 layer/step) and which parameter subsets are inside an active block \\u2014 assumed, needs confirmation.</item>\\n<item>[A7] Adam hyperparameters (\\u03b21, \\u03b22, \\u03b5, lr, schedule), weight-decay form and value, gradient-clipping norm \\u2014 assumed identical across optimizers, exact values need confirmation.</item>\\n<item>[A8] Update quantity for comparison (default: signed, bias-corrected m\\u0302/(\\u221av\\u0302+\\u03b5), with raw \\u0394_t = -\\u03b7\\u00b7that as tensor) \\u2014 assumed, needs confirmation, especially BAdam's moments in frozen blocks.</item>\\n<item>[A9] Numeric dtype at extraction and SVD (default: fp32 for captured \\u0394, fp64 accumulator for SVD; forward/backward can be bf16/fp16) \\u2014 assumed, needs confirmation.</item>\\n<item>[A10] Non-square matrix handling (default: Gram W W\\u1d40 or W\\u1d40 W; erank from smaller side) \\u2014 assumed, needs confirmation.</item>\\n<item>[A11] Statistical unit (default: per-(module, layer, step) snapshot, layer-index covariate, step-window random effect, paired test) \\u2014 assumed, needs confirmation.</item>\\n<item>[A12] Compute/storage budget \\u2014 CPU-only 24-core, no GPU, no network; a non-trivial run likely needs a separate runtime \\u2014 assumed, needs confirmation.</item>\\n<item>[A13] Reference \\\"BAdam\\\" semantics (published block-adaptive Adam for memory-efficient finetuning, ~2023\\u20132024) \\u2014 assumed, needs confirmation of paper/implementation to anchor against.</item>\\n<item>[A14] Pre-existing materials on disk \\u2014 none found; if track.md or other artefacts appear, design may be anchored to them \\u2014 needs confirmation.</item>\"], \"uncertainties\": [\"[U1] Whether the researcher will fix or defer each of A1\\u2013A14 before approving the full design.</item>\\n<item>[U2] Whether the spectral \\\"comparable\\\" criterion means statistically indistinguishable (paired test, null hypothesis of equal erank / tail-index) or \\\"within a stated tolerance band\\\" \\u2014 both affect sample-size and step-sampling density.</item>\\n<item>[U3] Whether per-(module, layer) comparison is per-step snapshot, per-token, or aggregated over a window \\u2014 affects snapshot count, storage budget, and statistical power.</item>\\n<item>[U4] Whether BAdam's reference implementation must be matched by parameter-selection rule (e.g., \\\"all params in active layers\\\" vs. \\\"only attention in active layers\\\"); this is a known fork-point across published variants.</item>\\n<item>[U5] Where the experiment will actually run given the CPU-only, no-network, no-checkpoints sandbox \\u2014 this is a feasibility gate, not a design micro-choice.</item>\\n<item>[U6] Whether the question targets the perturbation \\u0394 itself, or the bias-corrected normalized quantity m\\u0302/(\\u221av\\u0302+\\u03b5), or both; choice changes the null hypothesis materially.</item>\\n<item>[U7] Adequacy of M-P null + Pareto tail index as the heavy-tail criterion, versus alternatives such as the Kesten test or stable-distribution fit \\u2014 design implication in statistical-test selection.</item>\\n<item>[U8] Whether warm-up transients should be reported separately or excluded from the comparability claim; protocol detail with reporting impact.</item>\"]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-2f495b4e-94d4-4b5c-b02a-181acf33f440", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 14}
